commit 5f2d35c76c52c6bd23b6e4d8d325860e10651bbf
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 12:45:15 2026 -0500

    Correct the MGED who ordering regression
    
    The ordering test created order_first_sph1.s and order_second_sph2.s
    but attempted to draw shorter names that did not exist.  Both who calls
    therefore returned empty output, letting the comparison pass while path
    lookup errors accumulated in the log.
    
    Run the script through Tcl source mode, isolate its display state, and
    require an explicit pass marker.  Compare both draw orders with the
    expected sorted list so missing geometry cannot silently pass the test.

commit 148e11ff57becb834edbfbe104e138968d1ec2c0
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 10:13:19 2026 -0500

    Correct NIRT overlap plot endpoints
    
    The overlap plotting rewrite in e9efe16166 compared librt ray
    distances with NIRT view-depth values.  In 7.42.2 a redundant
    full-overlap draw masked that mismatch.  Commit b9bc08134f removed the
    redundant draw, exposing truncated or extended overlap lines beginning
    with 7.44.0.
    
    Keep clipping calculations in ray-distance coordinates.  Handle
    overlaps attached to an adjacent partition without reducing them to a
    point, and select the next overlap by entry rather than exit distance.
    
    Add a generic enclosing-box regression that checks the plotted overlap
    endpoints with both object preparation orders.

commit 86b1d79d9be9f5de981f03b288ece5062de23460
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 10:13:04 2026 -0500

    Make displayed object ordering deterministic
    
    Legacy display lists retain insertion order, so who and commands that
    consume ged_who_argv could see different object sequences based on draw
    order.  Since librt assigns region bits while preparing trees, that also
    made overlap claimant selection vary between otherwise identical NIRT
    shots.
    
    Sort displayed paths before reporting or returning them.  Add an MGED
    regression that exercises both draw orders.

