commit e91023f354a62395e3ac60963baa7c88de414893
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 5 13:50:34 2026 -0400

    Disable rtcmp tests for a BRLCAD_ENABLE_RUNTIME_DEBUG=OFF build
    
    rtcmp logging in librt is in the hot loop for rt_shootray, so
    even the enabled/disabled conditional check imposes about 1.5%
    performance overhead in an optimized build configuration.  Since
    that isn't acceptable when we're disabling debugging support for
    maximum performance, disable the tests in that particular case.

commit 303b90f7f1099d011bdc2320a36507695091df66
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 5 16:45:33 2026 +0000

    librt: handle empty and instanced trees during bounds traversal
    
    rt_gettree can succeed for an empty combination with no primitives,
    leaving its imported tree null.  The old traversal reached
    RT_CK_TREE.  With runtime checks enabled, that bombs and facetize's
    setjmp catches it.  Builds with runtime checks disabled compile out
    the magic check and dereference null instead.  This explains the
    different outcomes across build configurations.
    
    Return an error for null or NOP trees at every recursion level, so
    nested empty combinations also fail without a bomb.  Carry each
    member's accumulated transform when selecting a prepared solid;
    matching only the name chose the wrong instance when one primitive
    appeared at multiple locations.  Release imported combinations
    after recursion, use a stack tree for direct primitives, and return
    lookup errors instead of exiting the process.
    
    Cover empty and nested combinations, direct primitives, repeated
    transformed instances, and transforms through nested combinations.

