commit 917ce5554cbef146522b5910ef9824c9181ba440
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 18:24:40 2026 +0000

    Preserve primitive edits across failed saves and restores
    
    A failed checkpoint could discard the last saved state, and a
    failed revert could discard the current primitive. Restoring
    selected pipe or NMG geometry could also leave stale handles.
    
    Stage exports and imports before replacing live state, clear
    selections and refresh the keypoint after restore, and preserve
    SPH and REC types. Consume rejected edit input so a later command
    cannot reuse it, and prevent view-update counts from accumulating.
    
    Cover failed saves and restores, repeated revert, selected geometry,
    and default and non-default database units.

commit 58ab0d54966203d24ed076ddee75e3705d30a27e
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 17:39:17 2026 +0000

    Prevent rejected primitive edits from changing geometry
    
    Rejected height moves in TGC, CLINE, and EXTRUDE could replace
    valid geometry; NMG edge moves could partly change faces while
    reporting success. BOT edge splits could leave unused vertices, and
    malformed parameter text could partly overwrite seven primitives.
    
    Stage edits before applying them. Reject invalid REC and uniform
    scale inputs without changing geometry, and report scale failures.
    Cover these paths in default and non-default units, including CRLF
    parameter text and NMG selection remapping.

commit 13b06993494739a5e2a1471a7b4a42fa1ea1fc73
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 16:28:59 2026 +0000

    Prevent rejected ARB edits from corrupting geometry
    
    Mouse face drags and several ARB edit helpers could change points or
    planes before detecting invalid geometry. Subsequent edits then began
    from inconsistent state and could produce unexpected shape changes.
    
    Validate candidate geometry before committing it, restore state on
    rejected edits, and cover repeated mouse drags with non-default units.

