commit 14051845a314fe78ee36d29db9c902542444f223
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 20:49:41 2026 +0000

    facetize: add source-guided adaptive SPSR
    
    Fixed-size point dumps make Poisson reconstruction unreliable as a
    last-resort facetization method.  They can miss thin partitions while
    oversampling surfaces that are already well resolved, and an arbitrary
    point count does not show whether source characterization is complete.
    
    Seed reconstruction with stabilized Crofton samples.  Retain paired
    entry and exit normals, partition thickness, and ray identities so thin
    geometry contributes explicit local information instead of unrelated
    points.
    
    Add a bounded adaptive libbg driver around the existing upstream
    Poisson solver.  Each solve reports residual, density, normal, and
    surface-variation hints to a caller callback.  Facetize responds with
    exact source rays and validates partitions, endpoints, chord length,
    area, volume, and closed-manifold topology before accepting a result.
    
    Bound refinement by time, point, pass, and convergence limits.  Relax
    only chord and thin-partition thresholds when the source BoT is already
    known to be non-manifold.  Deprecate the fixed-array API, remove the
    intermediate point-sampling path, adapt pnts callers, and add focused
    coverage.  The vendored SPSR implementation remains unchanged.
    
    Use configured method priority for perturbation variants so an MDC-only
    run never invokes NMG.  Report finalization progress and retry counts
    while the fallback hierarchy is evaluated.

commit d6fa9372120a3a1e1c3c5f20d1dacb47e73f4b5f
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 20:49:17 2026 +0000

    libanalyze: replace marching cubes with adaptive MDC
    
    The legacy marching-cubes polygonizer sampled a uniform grid and could
    miss thin or high-aspect features, merge undersampled tunnels, and emit
    surfaces whose shared-edge winding was inconsistent.  Increasing the
    global resolution made those failures prohibitively expensive rather
    than addressing their local causes.
    
    Add a ray-driven manifold dual contouring API built on an adaptive
    octree.  Cache exact signs and Hermite edge crossings from librt
    partitions, place feature-preserving vertices with bounded QEF solves,
    and refine locally for thin walls, multiple crossings, interior
    surfaces, and ambiguous topology.  Build faces from shared crossings
    with deterministic winding and require closed manifold output.
    
    Back analyze_polygonize with the new implementation, expose MDC as a
    facetize method, and remove the obsolete polygonizer code, licensing,
    continuation sampler, and CM default.  Keep NMG available when polygon
    preservation is more important and it can successfully process the
    input.
    
    Document the Ju, Schaefer, and Warren algorithmic basis and the
    bottom-up Euler-characteristic escalation path.  Add coverage for thin
    walls, tunnels, overlapping CSG, toroidal cases, winding, resource
    limits, and the compatibility polygonalize entry point.

