commit 0f6db7016dbc779c9371cb095ace41603ceeae62
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 20:47:08 2026 +0000

    facetize: add supervised parallel primitive workers
    
    Primitive tessellation previously paid process and database setup
    costs per object and left the parent with limited visibility into work
    that timed out or died.  Large models consequently spent substantial
    time outside the tessellation algorithms themselves.
    
    Add long-lived supervised workers and a bounded scheduler for
    independent objects.  Divide CPUs between worker processes and each
    worker internal parallelism, reuse opened databases, and retain cache
    state across requests.
    
    Make result publication transactional.  A WRITE_STARTED acknowledgment
    closes the READY and PROCEED race, while the parent detects timeouts and
    abnormal exits, restarts workers, and records only completed object
    results.  Reuse temporary result databases without leaking state between
    requests.
    
    Add process and database-transfer helpers together with worker,
    recovery, and validation tests.  Document the parallel job control and
    its resource behavior.

commit cbffc1171bc1d2d432b8265ee2aff1b7b52d8b70
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 20:45:14 2026 +0000

    libbu: support resource-aware worker processes
    
    Large subprocess pools need to divide machine resources without allowing
    each worker internal parallelism to consume every CPU.  Add a
    process-local limit to bu_avail_cpus() and bu_parallel(), with atomic
    updates and coverage for applying and removing the limit.
    
    Make BU_MEM_AVAIL count FreeBSD reclaimable inactive and cache queues
    in addition to immediately free pages.  This prevents idle systems from
    appearing memory-starved to resource-aware algorithms and adds native
    sysctl checks for the reported values.
    
    Rename the private process.h to process_private.h.  This prevents the
    source header from shadowing the MSVC CRT header used by std::thread,
    which otherwise leaves _beginthreadex undeclared.

