commit de09372b73b005df7091abbb61c3cb4d905cc5d1
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 17 21:12:18 2026 +0000

    Fix BoT shots with origins inside mesh bounds
    
    Commit 7376385fd2 backed the HLBVH traversal origin by twice the
    soltab bounding radius to preserve entrance triangles.  Commit
    1d75918492 replaced that conservative distance with max(0, -r_min),
    assuming r_min reaches the solid boundary.  During rt_shootray,
    however, r_min can describe the current spatial partition cell.  A
    ray starting inside a BoT can enter that cell after entering the mesh.
    BVH culling then drops the entrance triangles, and segment assembly
    discards the exit hit without an entrance.  In an overlapping scene,
    ARS and native BoT differ because the ARS RPP test refreshes r_min.
    
    For origins inside the BoT BVH root box, move the traversal origin
    just beyond the box's entry face.  This retains the entrance facets
    without the excess traversal from a bounding radius backout.  Rays
    originating outside the box need no backout.  Share the calculation
    between scalar and vector shots, while keeping triangle intersections
    relative to the original ray origin.
    
    Five deterministic, single processor Generic_Twin.g renders per view
    had identical pixels with both backout methods.  The box method cut
    shot time by 3.5% from inside the flight deck console, 24.5% from
    inside a main strut, and 5.9% from inside a tire.  An exterior view
    differed by about 0.2% from the radius method.  Avoiding unnecessary BVH
    traversal more than offsets the extra box backout arithmetic for
    these interior views.
    
    Test direct ARS and BoT shots whose origins are inside the mesh,
    including vector shots, and an overlapping composite scene that
    reproduces the failure through rt_shootray without setting r_min
    manually.

