commit 416dbc260411362fcf10fdef499adcbaaa67395a
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 18:54:53 2026 +0000

    Serialize asynchronous MGED command execution
    
    Since d6c1f9d5c5 added asynchronous GED command execution, the GUI
    thread has pumped Tcl events while a worker owns shared GED, database,
    view, and display-list state. Only stdin was guarded, so a timer or GUI
    callback could start a second command concurrently.
    
    The search -exec path made this failure more severe by keeping its
    secondary interpreter in shared MGED state. A reentrant command could
    access or delete that interpreter from the wrong thread. Control-C also
    cleaned up the prompt without notifying the worker, after which another
    command could abort in TclStackFree with an incorrect freePtr.
    
    Route both Tcl spellings of every MGED command through one dispatcher
    and permit only one active command per mged_state. Keep interrupt and
    quit available while busy, and use execution-scoped atomic state for a
    cooperative search interruption.
    
    Create and delete the secondary search interpreter on the command
    worker, using a snapshot captured on the main Tcl thread. Do not invoke
    Tcl from a worker-side bomb hook.
    
    Preserve the caller Tcl result across the nested event pump. This is
    needed when an internal redraw follows a result-producing operation such
    as db_glob. Treat a temporarily unavailable display manager as an
    unsupported renderer probe rather than raising a background Tcl error.
    
    Mark rejected nested commands with a specific Tcl error code.  Display
    activation can then ignore that expected busy condition while still
    surfacing unrelated failures.

commit 019f59ac15626d5582d22a57cbde2a2b9f255d05
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 18:54:24 2026 +0000

    Accelerate legacy display-list path drawing
    
    The display-list design introduced by d7ef83f14c in July 2009 made each
    requested draw path a display root. Subsequent changes added a linear
    duplicate scan (3006fbdbd0), per-argument erase scans (2a1ac5bf00), and
    hierarchy splitting with repeated path parsing (ace8abe3b5).
    
    Together these made drawing N leaf paths O(N^2). Replacing paths below
    an existing aggregate root incurred a second quadratic pass because each
    new leaf replotted every scene object accumulated under the root.
    
    Maintain lazy private indexes for ordinary display roots and canonical
    scene paths. Endpoint sentinels detect callers using the legacy public
    list interface; instance-qualified and malformed paths retain parser and
    linked-list fallback behavior. Invalidate indexes on rename and clear.
    
    Replot and publish only newly appended scene objects. Fall back to one
    whole-root callback for clients lacking the per-scene callback.
    
    Also make scene removal advance safely past objects without private data
    and free the display-list ID belonging to each scene object.
    
    On m35.g, separate draws of 1,293 TGC paths fall from roughly 92 seconds
    to under one second, including repeated and aggregate-root replacement.
    
    Tests: ged drawing suite, MGED draw regressions, and repository checks.

commit 344ea00e49a5969352edb72f3de0b5a0dac21d1d
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 15:19:14 2026 +0000

    Retry interrupted external dependency post-processing
    
    The external file inventories were written before RPATH and path
    cleanup.  If plief failed fatally after files had been staged, their
    fresh timestamps made the next configure treat the raw copies as current
    and skip the failed work.
    
    Persist the set awaiting post-processing, merge that set into the next
    changed-file pass, and commit both inventories only after processing
    succeeds.  A retry now recopies clean bext inputs before applying the
    path transformations, while a successful pass removes the pending state.
    
