    updated 103 RPATHs, including the Tcl 8.6.18 launcher, and a subsequent
    no-change configure performed no restaging.  The relocated launcher
    loads Itcl 4.3.7 from the build tree.

commit fb3d03ae883bf52ed2b7aec8b4158b670808bc14
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 02:17:17 2026 +0000

    Replace ARB7 inside faceting with exact halfspaces
    
    An ARB7 coincident V5/V8 is incident to four planes. Moving those planes
    independently generally changes the local topology, so the result cannot
    in general remain an ARB7 or be forced into the fixed ARB8 face layout.
    Represent it directly as the intersection of its six translated
    halfspaces using ARBN, preserving exact face offsets without NMG
    tessellation or BOT approximation.
    
    Validate all triple-plane intersections before writing the result.
    Require each plane to remain active and require at least four
    non-coplanar feasible vertices, rejecting thicknesses that eliminate a
    face or collapse the volume.
    
    This replaces a path introduced in 869b018d03f (1994), when the old
    direct ARB point solver was changed to produce NMG topology. Commit
    91d12a95d1 (2000) subsequently converted that NMG to a BOT, and
    756081571e (2008) carried the implementation into libged. The path now
    fails to match the default ARB7 top face. It also contains a latent
    lifetime error from 5cf4f84357c (2021): nmg_extrude_cleanup() uses the
    shell after nmg_km() frees its model. Removing the obsolete NMG route
    eliminates both defects.
    
    Expand the MGED ARB regression to check exact inward and outward plane
    offsets, zero thickness, default and explicit small fixtures, ARBN
    tessellation, and collapsed-solid rejection. Source the test as one Tcl
    command so assertion failures cannot be hidden by MGED line-oriented
    stdin handling. Document the ARBN result and add a NEWS entry.
    
    Tests: rt_arb8_tests, regress-mged_3ptarb, regress-mged_arb, equal and
    unequal ARBN raytraces, and regress-repository.

commit 3e4eac25abcba36514bc756e28b59cd63be54fbe
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 13 19:35:40 2026 +0000

    Fix direct ARB face and edge-direction editing
    
    The libged edarb commands added in May 2013 inherited several latent
    argument-handling defects.  The two-angle edgedir form read the
    subcommand and object arguments instead of its rotation and fallback
    values.  Facedef retained an extrusion-derived type restriction despite
    having cases for ARB5 and ARB7, wrote a fixed-point sentinel beyond the
    caller argv array for the ARB7 side-face case, accepted out-of-range
    vertex selectors, and reported the object name rather than an invalid
    form.
    
    The ARB7 fixed-vertex special originated in the 1986 facedef
    implementation, where assigning cmd_args[5] was safe because cmd_args
    was a separate command buffer.  The April 1996 Tcl conversion changed
    that assignment to argv[5], making the five-argument ARB7 invocation an
    out-of-bounds write.  That conversion also omitted the required null
    terminators from two Tcl_AppendResult calls; the fixed-point message
    could consequently crash instead of completing the edit.  The 2013
    libged facedef copy preserved the unsafe sentinel technique.
    
    Use local fixed-point arguments, validate named vertices and public
    editing table indexes before array access, accept every recognized ARB4
    through ARB8 type, parse edge indexes completely, and read the actual
    angle arguments.  Centralize cleanup in the legacy MGED path so errors
    and quit do not leak its transformed internal object.
    
    Add regression coverage for both edgedir forms, every compact ARB type
    in direct facedef, both legacy and direct ARB7 fixed-point cases,
    malformed selectors, non-ARB input, and invalid public edit indexes.

