commit ffb4b9b7772c72f83186a265803bdf852b5b7ee2
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 13 17:25:27 2026 +0000

    Correct canonical ARB storage and centroid handling
    
    BRL-CAD compact ARBs have a stable public eight-slot convention: ARB4
    repeats V1 at V4 and its apex at V5-V8; ARB5 repeats V5 at V6-V8; ARB6
    repeats V5 at V6 and V7 at V8; ARB7 repeats V5 at V8.  The first make
    support for ARB4-ARB7 in 3b6c88b755 (February 1985) instead stored an
    ARB4 with V4 equal to V3.  Numerical type-in in abf2c2a86e (June 1985)
    used V4 equal to V1, so the two creation paths diverged at that point.
    The new ARB editor in ea7423aa0b (July 1985) explicitly encoded the
    convention above for every compact type.
    
    The specialized mk_arb4 added by d40fb36531 in September 1987 copied the
    make layout.  The 1993 import/export conversion in ade6618484, the 2008
    move into libged in b586ade52b, and the 2026 move into librt in
    70518d83e4 all preserved it.  Validator comments added by 56b03ac259 in
    April 2026 consequently described the generator layout as canonical, but
    the public contract, type-in path, repair mappings, and editing tables
    said otherwise.  The June 2026 editor cleanup in bf4e603b00 and the
    subsequent ARB point-edit repairs were not the source of the discrepancy
    and use the public convention.
    
    Make rt_arb_make and mk_arb4 produce the documented layout, and identify
    standard ARB4 through ARB8 storage by its complete tolerance-aware
    vertex-equivalence map.  Compute centroids from representative
    geometrically distinct vertices instead of the first N storage slots;
    the latter omitted a logical vertex for canonical ARB4 and ARB6.  With
    centroid behavior corrected, remove the compensating slot reshuffles
    from inside and remove the stale contradictory ARB6 mapping comment.
    
    Database import intentionally preserves raw slot ordering so old
    geometry round-trips without an implicit rewrite.  Geometrically valid
    nonstandard layouts continue through the convex-hull tessellation
    fallback, while the explicit repair operation canonicalizes them.  This
    retains compatibility with ARB4s emitted by historical make and mk_arb4
    implementations while keeping table-driven operations restricted to
    layouts they understand.
    
    Exercise default creation and libwdb factories for ARB4 through ARB8,
    standard and nonstandard centroid calculations, validation, DB5 round
    trips, repair canonicalization, canonical and fallback tessellation,
    inside generation, and canonical storage after the MGED permutation,
    mirror, extrusion, point, edge, face, and face-rotation edit paths.  The
    corresponding audit found no analogous factory encoding defect in ARB5
    through ARB8.

commit 0955bd15af464fd1c541059758ab9af3f0277ab2
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 14:29:21 2026 +0000

    Isolate concurrent MGED framebuffer sessions
    
    A standalone rtwizard fbserv can claim IPv4 port 5559 while
    Tcl_OpenTcpServer still reports success to MGED after binding only IPv6
    on that port. MGED then records 5559, but its rt child connects over
    IPv4 to rtwizard server and leaves MGED embedded framebuffer black.
    
    Inspect Tcl listener addresses and advance to another port unless MGED
    owns IPv4, retaining IPv6 whenever both families bind. Generate a token
    for each display manager and expose the active token to child tools, so
    a token-capable client reaching another BRL-CAD session is rejected.
    Continue accepting tokenless clients for the public listener legacy
    compatibility.

