commit bc94d9184ae895b9c9317ddf04b0c8df54125edb
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 12 15:57:55 2026 +0000

    Fix Archer tree handling for object names with spaces
    
    Archer's hierarchy member lookup used lt with a literal space delimiter.
    That implementation, introduced by 04c4de70c6 on 2016-04-21, cannot
    distinguish one object name containing spaces from several object names.
    As a result the hierarchy constructed bogus children for a valid
    combination.
    
    Walk the combination's structured Boolean tree instead, validating each
    operator while collecting leaves.  Also preserve leaf names as Tcl list
    elements when combinations pass through Archer's editable tree format,
    including matrix-bearing leaves.  This retains arbitrary legal database
    names without flattening their word boundaries.

