commit aa76ac4476aea38b8f5315c712706c75b5980239
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 14:21:29 2026 +0000

    Add optional Xmin build support
    
    Xmin (https://github.com/starseeker/Xmin) is a small, self-contained X11 server
    and basic client library harness intended for headless testing of X graphical
    stacks.  It can display (with patching of the libraries in question to build
    against its client support) the Tk and Qt graphical toolkits.
    
    This is a testing only configuration, but it has proven useful on a couple
    separate occasions now so it seems easier to set up our build system to support
    using it than require hacking it in every time.
    
    Accordingly, we add an explicit XMIN X11 provider without changing the default
    system-X11 behavior.  Require Tk, OpenGL, Qt, display-manager, and TclCAD
    consumers to use one consistent X11 ABI, and forward the selected Xmin SDK and
    toolkit patch configuration into managed bext builds.
    
    We also teach the X, GLX, Tk software-rendering, TclCAD, MGED, and Qt
    dependency setup to consume the imported Xmin targets.

