commit 39cab50e451ee4e979c25d177310d6414924370c
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 06:49:11 2026 -0400

    Fix lcov build annot test crash
    
    In src/librt/primitives/annot/annot.c:2058, this is unsafe:
    
    VMOVE(polygon[polygon_count++], vp->pt[i]);
    
    VMOVE is a macro that evaluates its destination three times—once for X,
    Y, and Z. Consequently, polygon_count increments three times. Starting
    at 1, it writes approximately:
    
    polygon[1][X]
    polygon[2][Y]
    polygon[3][Z]  /* outside point_t polygon[3] */
    
    The final write corrupts the stack. Under the coverage build, it
    overwrites the return address of annot_segment_mesh(). The debugger
    showed that address becoming 0x4042000000000000, the IEEE-754
    representation of 36.0, confirming that a point coordinate was written
    over it. The segfault then occurs as the function returns at line
    2080.
    
    This explains why lcov could fail while other configurations pass:
    coverage instrumentation changes the stack layout enough for the
    overflow to hit the saved return address.

