commit 51abddb65631db3f00a222c523f97ffa39b31b86
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 17:15:17 2026 +0000

    Use TinyGLTF v3 for native glTF I/O
    
    Migrate the native glTF readers and BoT exporter from TinyGLTF's v2 C++
    interface to the v3 C API.  Share checked accessor handling between gltf-g
    and the GCV plugin.
    
    Constrain external asset reads to the source model's canonical directory,
    including protection against symlink escapes.  Limit input files, individual
    allocations, and parser memory, retain encoded images without decoding, and
    avoid preserving unused extension data unless requested.
    
    Rewrite BoT export using the v3 POD model and writer API.  Correct index
    accessor counts, validate face indices and buffer sizes, align combined
    buffer data, and initialize exporter state reliably.
    
    TinyGLTF v3 validates accessor component types against the glTF 2.0
    specification.  By default this removes support for BRL-CAD's non-standard
    DOUBLE POSITION accessors: models written with `bot dump -F` are no longer
    accepted by the native v3 readers.  We have patched our bext copy of
    tinygltf to support reading back in old files written with the -F option,
    but it is longer supported as an output mode since that formatting is
    non-compliant (other readers do not support it - that problem has already
    been seen in the wild - and tinygltf upstream no longer supports it either.

