commit d985e5e1113865228b6cf350685ff7989c991c20
Author: Christopher Sean Morrison <brlcad@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 6 07:59:12 2026 -0400

    significant change to DPIX file format to assume/require on-disk encoding to be network-order bytes.
    
    this fixes a portability incompatibility bug where a little-endian system would write out host-order and another big-endian would read the DPIX flipped.
    
    only able to take this liberty because there is not any published documentation on what the dpix file format is or what tools like dpix-pix are expecting.  does open a can of worms though on all the other signal processing tools that currently read/write host doubles -- probably should introduce a byte-swap option on all of them just as a safety net.

