commit 203bba3617a1c03723f9686b17675e1b0d61598e
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 5 08:50:28 2026 -0400

    Keep MGED display-list callbacks on the GUI thread
    
    Interactive GED commands run on a worker so long operations do not block
    Tk, but their display-list callbacks inherited the worker thread. OpenGL
    contexts are thread-affine, so glGenLists could crash when display lists
    were enabled.
    
    Record the GUI Tcl thread and synchronously marshal display-list and
    refresh callbacks through its event queue. Continue servicing events
    during staged shutdown so a worker cannot deadlock waiting for a queued
    callback. Use each display manager context for list allocation,
    compilation, and deletion instead of the globally current DMP.
    
    This preserves asynchronous geometry work while keeping all GL access on
    the owning thread.

