    binary searched for failure objects when encountered - the latter behavior is
    extremely slow when there are lots of failures.  Instead, launch a subprocess
    and pipe objects to it, managing and at need restarting that subprocess without
    the hack of batching command line args to communiate what needs processing.
    Use a communication protocol to make it clear what data is passing between
    parent and child.
    
    Use improved bu_process polling and termination APIs, allowing us to
    remove the private vendored subprocess.h implementation.

