commit 7b7c0cb4d08298dc9677e296b5595f154d2cb57c
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 20:56:45 2026 -0400

    Improve OpenNURBS I/O robustness
    
    OpenNURBS has two concrete concurrency hazards:
    
    - ON::Begin() uses unsynchronized global initialization state.
    - Model reads reach Unix localtime(), which uses process-wide state.
    
    Added a mutex-based protection into a shared transactional archive reader
    in src/librt/primitives/brep/ brep.cpp:2352, while improving the
    branch’s version to:
    
    - Check ONX_Model::Read() and every recovered component.
    - Publish an internal BREP only after complete success.
    - Protect both database imports and base64 adjust reads.
    - Preserve the old BREP when adjustment fails.
    - Free decoded base64 buffers correctly.
    - Fix backward seeking and overflow handling in the in-memory archive.
    
    The existing tests did not directly cover BREP archive I/O. Added
    src/librt/tests/brep_io.cpp:1, covering round trips, concurrent imports,
    base64 adjustment, truncated archives, and arbitrary invalid data.

