commit df19156341576b11d34501a5b321956033c47352
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 12:09:18 2026 -0400

    Work on fixing ARB5 moving point 5 editing
    
    User report was that moving point 5 on an arb5 also moves point 1.
    
    Root cause analysis from AI was that ARB point-move menu handlers
    (`arb5_edge`, `arb6_edge`, `arb7_edge`) pre-remapped the menu-arg value
    (8 = pt5, 9 = pt6, 11 = pt5 on ARB7) into the point storage location
    (4/6) BEFORE `rt_arb_edit()` ran its dispatch.  `rt_arb_edit()`'s
    ARB5/6/7 case tests `edit_type` against the `RT_ARB{5,6,7}_MOVE_POINT_*`
    constants (values 8/9/11). With the menu value clobbered to 4, the POINT
    branch never fired and control fell through to the EDGE path (`earb5[4]`
    = edge 15), dragging pt1 along with pt5.
    
    Interactive testing doesn't result in the arb5 point 5 moving at all in
    MGED, but it's not clear if that's a side effect of this change or other
    breakage tied to the shift to librt editing. Go ahead and apply the
    suggested change, since even if it's not fully sufficient itself it's
    likely the logic in question is involved.
    
    Add a follow-on TODO item to investigate and fix ARB5 point 5 moving not
    being responsive.  Also make a more general note that we need to test
    the shift to librt-based primitive editing extensively for the next
    release.

