commit f1c4f4f03ba96e58407391f6e35b2acb6a44181e
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 19 16:30:41 2026 -0400

    Use info from parent Tcl interp
    
    The info complete command checks if a string is a syntactically complete
    Tcl command (i.e. if the string has balanced braces, brackets, and
    quotes.)  Use the info command from the parent interp in case info gets
    aliased as something else in the other. "info complete" operates
    strictly as a lexical parser rule check, so it doesn't matter which Tcl
    interp makes the validity determination.
    
    Report was an 'expected boolean value but got ""' error from an
    integrating application - a user redefinition of the info command in the
    lower level interp is a possible source of that message.

