commit aa7f93a8aa5316ee21879452f8c3c9b2c9c5c7bd
Author: Christopher Sean Morrison <brlcad@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 00:13:34 2026 -0400

    speed up heavy-CSG rendering (10-20%) with a bit-test filter.
    
    this is a bloom-style filter meaning it's not conclusive when a bit is
    set (so we keep scanning as before), but a missing bit proves the
    solid is absent (so we can stop early).  no false negatives or
    semantic changes to tracing, just a nifty speed up when models get
    complex.
    
    on small models with less than 64 solids, it's actulaly exact, but
    then the gain is expected to be minimal.
    
    in testing benchmark was relativley unchanged, but havoc improved more
    than 12%.

commit 0ff6b79d2666c67405be1953bebfa528dbda9760
Author: Christopher Sean Morrison <brlcad@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 00:07:32 2026 -0400

    only insert unique regions, big speed-up on heavy CSG trees.
    
    by only inserting unique we no longer end up inserting and iterating
    over duplicate st_regions during prep, once per solid leaf.  by
    eliminating this during prep, we speed up ray trace shot time during
    region traversals (e.g., during boolean weaving).
    
    this prep-time region dedupe doesn't make a difference on benchmark
    models, but is another 5% improvement on havoc.

