    libbg: enable LBFGS++ optimization for Geogram remeshing
    
    Add an MIT-licensed LBFGS++ adapter for Geogram's CVT optimizer,
    replacing the upstream HLBFGS implementation (which we cannot use due to
    licensing issues.)  This restores the intended quasi-Newton phase, which
    previously fell back to additional Lloyd iterations because no usable
    optimizer was available.
    
    Generic_Twin testing with an example Generic_Twin mesh shows a modest
    improvement in average triangle quality at roughly 30% higher runtime
    and memory use.  The overall timings remain comparable, making the
    tradeoff appropriate for a quality-oriented remeshing operation.
    
    Preserved fixed-iteration and progress-callback behavior, added focused
    optimizer tests, and recorded the exact upstream revision and license.
    
    Removed the unused legacy C/Fortran liblbfgs vendor tree.

