    Faster CMake logic should be ready.
    
    This work is an attempt to dramatically speed up BRL-CAD's configure
    process.  There are many pieces to that puzzle, but among them is
    parallel processing of the BRL-CAD bext dependency files - for that we
    need the new versions of plief and strclear.
    
    This is a major change to our configure process, so it will likely need
    some shakedown, but testing so far has shown configure times dropping
    from multiple minutes to around a minute or a little less in standard
    build configurations with a pre-existing bext build to stage.

