    More MSVC optimizations, add in first cut at validator
    
    When testing with MSVC, it's far faster to us the ninja generator than to write
    out full projects for each test.  However, the obvious concern in that case is
    whether or not the test is actually representative of what the compile
    enviornment set up by the MSVC project would see.
    
    We need two things - env setup so we match the MSVC environment, and a way to
    check that we are in fact getting the test results we should be getting. That
    means a comparator for different CMake run outputs - the "probe_validation"
    portion of this commit.

commit c0fe9c6238a7da0f64eb09a2945fad7aaa871ca3
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 11:38:41 2026 -0400

    Consolidate and modernize our OpenGL CMake
    
    The X11 OpenGL path on the Mac is currently (07/2026) not reliably working, so
    until the situation improves we won't try to build OpenGL there.  Mixing in the
    Aqua OpenGL with X11 won't work, and we don't want to end up detecting that and
    enabling OpenGL incorrectly.
    
    Also switching to having one top level OpenGL find_package handle everything,
    as well as using the modern target definitions in our targets in lieu of
    specifiying headers and libraries manually.

