commit 2eb5a44f830d1154c51efe9a1a2379337952157d
Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 23:18:31 2026 -0400

    Improved configure-time batching and bext postprocessing
    
    Reduce configure-time overhead by batching more CMake status output and
    third-party dependency processing work.
    
    Key changes include:
    
    - Batch compiler/probe result reporting instead of emitting one message
      sequence per check.
    - Summarize missing executable man pages once at the end of configure,
      with the full list available in verbose output.
    - Add path-form handling for bundled third-party cleanup so symlinked
      and real bext paths are both scrubbed reliably.
    - Use plief change reporting and selective RPATH updates when available,
      preserving useful existing $ORIGIN entries while replacing stale build
      paths.
    - Keep strclear as a separate residual stale-path cleanup pass and label
      its output/log entries accordingly.
    - Batch strclear processing for binary, data, and text file groups and
      write detailed per-configure and cumulative logs under CMakeFiles.
    - Reduce per-file configure chatter for third-party staging and install
      rule setup, replacing it with counts and detailed logs where needed.
    
    On the tested Linux configuration configure time dropped to less than 50
    seconds with these changes. The staged bext binary set remains the same,
    with unchanged NEEDED and SONAME metadata; RPATH/RUNPATH differences are
    limited to the intended preservation of valid $ORIGIN entries and
    removal of stale bext install paths.

